<title>USA: Brent crude slips in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude slips in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude slipped in late U.S. paper trading on Thursday, trade sources said.</p>
<p>Five partial September cargoes changed hands, four at $18.63 and one at $18.62 for a total of 600 lots.</p>
<p>September Brent went out at $18.68 on London's IPE.</p>
<p>August/September Brent traded at plus 8.5 cents a barrel, while September/October was talked at minus eight to five cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
